P-C': well-formed EC: the dual has no critical siphon (every T-trap contains an internal cycle)
P-G: (H1)-(H3): minimal siphons = semiflow supports implies every minimal siphon is a union of MIPS and every MIPS lies in a minimal siphon
P-K10: EC, connected, (H1), (H2), m = #source complexes: if s = m-1 then for k = 1 and 3 seeded random rational k, ker A_k is a line spanned by a positive vector; if s >= m, some tested k has no positive steady state
P-K11: EC with balanced joins, connected, (H1), (H2): [N has a positive steady state for all tested k] = [N* has one for all tested kappa] = [s = #clusters - 1] (k, kappa: all ones and 3 seeded random rationals)
G-2.1: all networks: q = beta* + delta* (q = n - s, beta* = n - m* + l*); if N* WR then l* + delta* <= q; q = 1 and N* WR => l* = 1, delta* = 0, dual graph one directed cycle
G-2.2: WR+(H3): source rows distinct, product rows distinct; N* WR iff {source rows} = {product rows}; then m* = n, l* = c(pi), delta* = q - c(pi), each pi-orbit sums to a conservation law; q = 1 => pi one n-cycle
G-7.1: WR + (H1) + every row of Ye has sum <= 1: disjoint cycles (each complex source of one reaction), deficiency 0, no critical siphon; with (H3) every complex is one species
